[[:db/retract 17592186088155 :question/answer-fields 17592186085584] {:db/id 17592186184190 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-23470b63-10f9-5736-89ca-b9c89f21d360"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-23470b63-10f9-5736-89ca-b9c89f21d360" :question/id #uuid "23470b63-10f9-5736-89ca-b9c89f21d360" :question/math-academy-id "q-347226" :question/problem "The fifth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\n{P}_{5}(x)=6+12(x-1)+9(x-1)^{2}+4(x-1)^{3}+\\frac{5}{4}(x-1)^{4}+\\frac{3}{10}(x-1)^{5}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${f}^{(5)}(1)?$\n\n${f}^{(5)}(1)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of $(x-1)^{5}$ is given by $\\frac{{f}^{(5)}(1)}{5!}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{f}^{(5)}(1)}{5!} & =\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ \\frac{{f}^{(5)}(1)}{120} & =\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ {f}^{(5)}(1) & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-448b4c89-4022-50f5-af1b-27d8086bba6c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-448b4c89-4022-50f5-af1b-27d8086bba6c" :answer-field/id #uuid "448b4c89-4022-50f5-af1b-27d8086bba6c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2650b1f4-0b37-597f-9c58-6fa55b3f1254" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2650b1f4-0b37-597f-9c58-6fa55b3f1254"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2650b1f4-0b37-597f-9c58-6fa55b3f1254" :answer/id #uuid "2650b1f4-0b37-597f-9c58-6fa55b3f1254" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186088155 :question/problem "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=6v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=6.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1235c3ee-01a6-5118-9232-ffc94935dca5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1235c3ee-01a6-5118-9232-ffc94935dca5" :answer-field/id #uuid "1235c3ee-01a6-5118-9232-ffc94935dca5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b29172ef-23dc-5743-a67c-26d08a2db9a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0207d956-c871-5c34-8c83-998c0d45f1b7" "answer-b29172ef-23dc-5743-a67c-26d08a2db9a3" "answer-b113d288-13d0-5627-8a97-e292566d6fa3" "answer-4b10917c-7b50-5beb-9269-5fa579194a74" "answer-240b2653-be6a-543b-87fa-bc567dfdb80c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0207d956-c871-5c34-8c83-998c0d45f1b7" :answer/id #uuid "0207d956-c871-5c34-8c83-998c0d45f1b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b29172ef-23dc-5743-a67c-26d08a2db9a3" :answer/id #uuid "b29172ef-23dc-5743-a67c-26d08a2db9a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b113d288-13d0-5627-8a97-e292566d6fa3" :answer/id #uuid "b113d288-13d0-5627-8a97-e292566d6fa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 48 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b10917c-7b50-5beb-9269-5fa579194a74" :answer/id #uuid "4b10917c-7b50-5beb-9269-5fa579194a74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-240b2653-be6a-543b-87fa-bc567dfdb80c" :answer/id #uuid "240b2653-be6a-543b-87fa-bc567dfdb80c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100931 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ca3460ff-fc6a-5037-a239-c26e4d66f531"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ca3460ff-fc6a-5037-a239-c26e4d66f531" :question/id #uuid "ca3460ff-fc6a-5037-a239-c26e4d66f531" :question/math-academy-id "q-81675" :question/problem "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ about $x=0$ is" :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =0+2\\cdot x+0\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+(-8)\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =2x-\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ee929d99-8395-520f-9fff-986b822a2550"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ee929d99-8395-520f-9fff-986b822a2550" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee929d99-8395-520f-9fff-986b822a2550" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-39fd6de8-6f95-5631-b334-32efddd1b965" :answer-field/choices ["answer-027a3f93-4382-5743-ab79-cccedb84b4ff" "answer-74bb8982-17bf-5df0-9881-6ae28b946b4e" "answer-352c3c2e-08c8-5fe6-a400-f998e25210c8" "answer-39fd6de8-6f95-5631-b334-32efddd1b965" "answer-3294f31c-d9c8-59dc-9bfa-e056c7a88aee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-027a3f93-4382-5743-ab79-cccedb84b4ff" :answer/id #uuid "027a3f93-4382-5743-ab79-cccedb84b4ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74bb8982-17bf-5df0-9881-6ae28b946b4e" :answer/id #uuid "74bb8982-17bf-5df0-9881-6ae28b946b4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-352c3c2e-08c8-5fe6-a400-f998e25210c8" :answer/id #uuid "352c3c2e-08c8-5fe6-a400-f998e25210c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39fd6de8-6f95-5631-b334-32efddd1b965" :answer/id #uuid "39fd6de8-6f95-5631-b334-32efddd1b965" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3294f31c-d9c8-59dc-9bfa-e056c7a88aee" :answer/id #uuid "3294f31c-d9c8-59dc-9bfa-e056c7a88aee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-4e1d8ee8-9c39-5df9-b4e1-810c5e0e4229" :activity/id #uuid "4e1d8ee8-9c39-5df9-b4e1-810c5e0e4229" :activity/title "Quiz 4" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-edaa7a81-43c4-5fba-ba12-3da5d171195f" "step-cbe80e64-6cb2-5624-93e4-aec8efbbce68" "step-506e12af-bf04-5946-bba6-af1152b8d511" "step-9df23eb1-7334-5ee3-99e0-0928ef712e13" "ste